    "verdict": "proven",
    "verdict_reasoning": "The experimental results strongly support the core hypothesis. Real variables (Population and Area) demonstrate excellent conformity to Benford's Law with very low MAD scores (0.0027 and 0.0063), aligning closely with theoretical expectations as required. Crucially, the derived density ratios and synthetic control datasets exhibit distinct deviations (MAD > 0.008 for Density, significantly higher for synthetics) compared to the real variables, confirming the method's ability to differentiate between naturally occurring data and anomalous entries. While the Chi-square test flagged 'Significance' for Area and Density due to the large sample size rather than poor conformity, the primary success criteria regarding MAD scores and the differentiation trend are overwhelmingly met.",
